     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Thursday, February 11, 2016 at 3:58:37 PM UTC-5, Daniel Lee wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div>Hi Chris,<br><br></div>The format used to read from the data file isn&#39;t quite native R. I believe technical details on what&#39;s allowed is in the CmdStan manual, but it&#39;s really not worth reading.<br><br></div>The quick fix is to change x to:<br>x &lt;- <br>structure(c(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 3, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2, 1),<br>.Dim = c(15, 1))<br><br></div>If you&#39;re using R to export the data, I&#39;d suggest using rstan&#39;s stan_rdump() function. It handles edge cases better than just using dump() in R.<br><br><br></div>Daniel<br><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Feb 11, 2016 at 3:51 PM, Christopher Kedzie <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">christophe...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to stan, so apologies if I am missing something obvious here.</div><div><br></div><div>I am trying to fit a simple poisson regression. My model compiles but when I try to run I get the following error:</div><div><br></div><div><div>Exception: data x value  beyond int range</div><div>Diagnostic information: </div><div>stan_2.9.0/src/stan/io/dump.hpp(522): Throw in function bool stan::io::dump_reader::next()</div><div>Dynamic exception type: boost::exception_detail::clone_impl&lt;boost::exception_detail::error_info_injector&lt;std::invalid_argument&gt; &gt;</div><div>std::exception::what: data x value  beyond int range</div></div><div><br></div><div>The model is:</div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>transformed parameters  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"c